Crypto Structural Anomaly & State Override Detection Engine (CSAD)
​Overview
​CSAD is an advanced computational forensics and structural audit framework designed to detect undocumented hardcoded overrides, asynchronous ledger decoupling, and invisible shadow-settlement paths within core digital asset exchange engines and distributed node binaries.
​While traditional security audits and public Proof-of-Reserves ledgers monitor surface-level API endpoints, CSAD targets deep compiled-node logic, low-level execution subroutines, and hidden state alteration vectors.
​Core Features & Modules
​1. Cross-Margin Contagion Loop Detector (cmcl_detector.py)
​Analyzes real-time order matching engine data to trace automated cascading liquidation loops.
​Identifies unauthorized collateral routing between primary trading books and internal treasury accounts during high-volatility events.
​2. Node Binary Anomaly Analyzer (node_binary_analyzer.rs)
​Scans compiled C++/Rust core node binaries for Hardcoded Root-State Overrides (HRSO).
​Flags hidden administrative subroutines capable of altering account balances without generating public multi-signature logs or event traces.
​3. Ledger Synchronization Audit Engine (ledger_sync_audit.py)
​Compares front-end order book states against deep database ledgers.
​Detects instances of Asynchronous Ledger Decoupling (ALD) where internal balances disconnect from live blockchain verification chains.
​Technical Architecture & Methodology
​Forensic Scope: Low-level state logic and memory execution mapping.
​Target Environment: Centralized and decentralized digital asset exchange infrastructure.
​Objective: Deliver non-falsifiable technical evidence of structural vulnerabilities and ensure absolute operational integrity.
